 "_readme": [
  "Where a newsroom actually sits. Zooming the map onto a city shows that city's own",
  "press, so we need to know that the NZZ is a Zurich paper and the Luzerner Zeitung a",
  "Lucerne one.",
  "",
  "Keys are ISO 3166-1 numeric country codes; inside each country, a lowercase substring",
  "of the outlet name maps to a city in data/cities.json. Scoping by country keeps",
  "ambiguous names apart — 'The Nation' is a Lahore paper in Pakistan and a Lagos paper",
  "in Nigeria.",
  "",
  "Outlets whose name already contains their city (Luzerner Zeitung, Toronto Star,",
  "Bangkok Post) are matched automatically and do not need an entry here.",
  "",
  "Adding your local paper is a one-line pull request — see CONTRIBUTING.md."
 ],
